# Varza design

Varza gets people off the couch to play, socialize, and meet someone new. Rainy Saturday, bored at home, open Varza, see what is on nearby, go. The look is calm and quiet: light grey page, white cards, soft grey borders, big type. Color is for status only. Every page uses the same header and footer.

Copy: follow the `varza-voice` skill before any user-facing text. Screen structure: follow the `varza-ux` skill. A new activity: follow the `varza-new-activity` skill.

Do not describe Varza as a tool for ten friends, a small crew, or a WhatsApp replacement. Do not mention WhatsApp on the homepage. The share button inside a game may still say "Share on WhatsApp".

## Voice

Warm, social, a bit cheeky. Second person. Plain English. No exclamation marks. Buttons are verbs: "I'm in", "See what's on", "Start a game". The long before-and-after list is in the voice skill.

Spirit: "Bored at home? Go play."

Locked strings, until a copy change updates the tests too: "Your next game", "Open near you", "Vote on a time", "Availability", "Best time", "Your RSVP", "Lock in this time", "This time has passed".

## Color

Tokens live in `resources/css/app.css` as CSS variables and are mapped in `tailwind.config.js`. The page is light grey (`canvas`, `#F5F5F7`), text is near-black (`ink`), secondary text is grey (`ink-muted`, `ink-faint`), soft fills are `mist` (a step darker than the page), and borders are `line`. `success` and `success-soft` are the only green, and only for status. Do not color a link, a button, a logo, or a page with pitch green.

- The page, header, and mobile nav use `canvas`. The header keeps a bottom `line` border and `shadow-card` so the bar still reads on the grey. Cards, sheets, menus, and inputs stay white with a 1px `line` border, a large radius, and `shadow-card`. No heavy shadow, no gradient, no mesh.
- Pitch green is for status only: spots left, you're in, a warning, a danger. It is not a button color.
- Primary buttons, including "I'm in", are `bg-ink` with white text. Hover is `bg-ink/90`. Secondary buttons are `bg-mist` with ink text and a `line` ring, so they read on both the grey page and a white card. Focus rings are ink.
- Chips share one style through `x-ui.chip`: white, a `line` ring, ink text, at least 44px tall. The selected chip is `bg-ink` with white text. Use it for filters, the sport picker, activity options, form choices, homepage activities, and the activity name. Neutral badges, including "Public game", are white with a `line` ring and ink text. Green is status only: spots left, you're in, best time, a warning, a danger. Each of these has to stay visible on `canvas` and on white.
- A highlighted card (the next game, the best time) uses `bg-highlight` (`#F0FAF3`) and a single 1px `border-highlight-line`. No second border, no 2px outline, no ring, no shadow. Text stays ink. Primary stays near-black.
- Area pills are solid `bg-white`. No translucent fill and no backdrop blur.
- Body and helper text is `text-base`. `text-sm` is for badges, chips, and timestamps.
- People lists use a 44px avatar. A smaller avatar is only for a tight meta row, such as the header or a note next to its time.
- Page titles sit in the main column with `x-ui.page-header`. There is no extra bordered title bar. The footer is `max-w-content`. Only the footer adds space for the mobile nav.
- Neutrals: `canvas` page background, `ink` text, `ink-muted` secondary text, `ink-faint` placeholders, `line` borders, `sand` inside illustrations.
- Status: `success` (same green family), `warn`, `danger`, each with a `soft` background.
- Do not color a chip, a button, or a page with an activity accent.
- Do not use Tailwind's default rainbow classes (`indigo`, `orange`, `sky`, `rose`, and the rest). Extra hues go through an `--activity-*` token.

Logged-in screens use the grey canvas and white cards. No mesh, grain, or glass there.

## Marketing pages

The homepage uses the same tokens as the app. The hero and the closing line are `text-5xl` or `text-6xl font-bold tracking-tight`. Section titles are `text-3xl font-bold`. No mesh, grain, dark band, or glass.

## Typography

Inter, self-hosted in `public/fonts`, with the system sans fallback. Weights in use: 400, 500, 600, 700.

Inter, weights 400, 500, 600, 700. Page titles are `text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight`. Section and card titles are `text-lg font-bold`. Card facts are `text-lg`. Body and helper copy is `text-base` with `text-ink-muted`. `text-sm` is for badges, chips, and timestamps. Links are ink with an underline, not green. Do not set a font below 16px on inputs (iOS zoom).

## Spacing

Use the 4px scale: 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 12, 16 (`--space-*`). Stack related items with `gap` or `space-y-*`, not ad-hoc margins between siblings. Page content is `max-w-content` (40rem), padded `px-4` on mobile. Touch targets are at least 44px (`min-h-11`).

## Radius and shadow

- `rounded-control` (14px) on inputs, buttons, and chips.
- `rounded-card` (28px) on cards. Photos inside a card are `rounded-2xl`.
- `rounded-full` on badges, avatars, and activity chips.
- `shadow-card` is a faint lift on white cards and the header. `shadow-lift` is for menus and dialogs. A 1px `line` border is still the edge. Buttons have no shadow.

## Icons

One set: [Lucide](https://lucide.dev) (ISC). Outline, 24px viewBox, stroke 2, `currentColor`, round caps and joins.

Render icons only as `<x-ui.icon name="..." />`. Paths in that component are Lucide. Do not add `blade-heroicons`, `blade-lucide-icons`, emoji, or one-off SVG icons in a page. Add a new Lucide path to `x-ui.icon` when a screen needs a new symbol.

Info-row names the UX skill expects: `calendar`, `clock`, `map-pin`, `users`, `bar-chart`, `sun`, `home`. Icon color is `ink-faint`.

## Motion

A small kit, CSS and Alpine only. No GSAP, Motion One, anime.js, AOS, or other animation libraries. Durations 150–400ms.

- Press: `.motion-press` scales to 0.98 on active, 150ms. Buttons already use it.
- Success pop: `.motion-pop`, a one-shot scale from 0.96 to 1, 200ms.
- Sliding active indicator: `.motion-slide`, transform, 200ms.
- Count tick: a number changes with a short vertical slide, about 200ms.
- Skeleton pulse: `.motion-skeleton`, opacity only, about 1.2s, and only while loading.
- View transitions: `.motion-view` opts one element in. Do not set it on two elements.
- No hero entrance. Keep feedback to the press scale.

`prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` is handled globally in `app.css`. Do not override it. Under reduced motion: no transform, no pulse, no entrance, instant state. The logged-in app does not use the hero entrance.

## Components

Use these Blade components instead of restyling raw elements.

| Component | Use |
| --- | --- |
| `x-ui.shell` | The one chrome: `x-ui.header`, the page, `x-ui.footer`, and the logged-in mobile nav. Every layout uses it. |
| `x-ui.wordmark` | The mark plus the word Varza. Link it home. |
| `x-ui.page-header` | The title of a screen, with optional subtitle and `actions` slot. |
| `x-ui.section` | A labeled group on a page. |
| `x-ui.card` | A white surface for a form, a detail block, or a poll option. Padding is `p-4 sm:p-6`. Pass `highlight` for the soft green best-time card. |
| `x-ui.button` | `primary`, `secondary`, `ghost`, `danger`. Pass `href` for a link. Primary is the one next step. Includes `.motion-press`. |
| `x-ui.info-row` | Icon plus text. Variants: `date`, `time`, `place`, `spots`, `level`, `outdoor`, `indoor`. `place` takes `href` for the map. |
| `x-ui.header` | The one header. Logged out: wordmark, Log in, Sign up. Logged in: Games, What's on, Start a game, account menu. |
| `x-ui.game-card` | Photo, title, status chip, info rows, host, price, I'm in. Map link sits outside the title link. |
| `x-ui.chip` | The one chip. A link, a radio label (`for`), or a static name. Selected is ink. |
| `x-ui.label` | Every control's label. |
| `x-ui.input` | Text, email, password, number, date, and poll datetimes. |
| `x-ui.select` | A native select when there are many short options and chips would wrap into a mess. |
| `x-ui.textarea` | Notes and descriptions. |
| `x-ui.error` | Validation messages for one field. |
| `x-ui.badge` | Status such as "Best time". Tones: `pitch`, `warn`, `neutral`. Presets: `full`, `beginners`, `indoor`, `outdoor`. "Public game" is neutral. |
| `x-ui.sport-chip` | The activity name. Delegates to `x-ui.chip`. |
| `x-ui.avatar` | Photo, or initials. People lists are 44px. `size="meta"` is the small row. `size="photo"` is the profile picture. |
| `x-ui.empty-state` | A titled empty list with an illustration and an optional action. |
| `x-ui.checkbox` | Remember me, reminders, and remove photo. |
| `x-ui.file` | The one file input, for a game photo or an avatar. |
| `x-ui.modal` | Confirm dialogs. |
| `x-ui.status` | A short success line, such as a reset link sent. |
| `x-ui.icon` | The Lucide set. |
| `x-illustrations.hero` | Landing hero only. |
| `x-illustrations.sport` | Unused on the game card. A game shows its photo, or `public/images/sports/{sport}.svg`. |
| `x-illustrations.empty` | Empty states. Variants: `games`, `public`, `invites`, `votes`. |

Game photos are the host's upload, or the grey picture in `public/images/sports/`. Empty states stay inline SVG. No stock photos, no hotlinked images.

## Checklist

Point at the one primary action. Facts are info rows. Grey page, white cards, near-black primary, color only for status. Then run the `varza-voice` and `varza-ux` checklists.
